{"id":"4396538a738cd422","group":"58","path":"58/batch05/58-df-skein-relation.md","title":"Skein Relation","display":"df-skein-relation — Skein Relation","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-skein-relation","aliases":["58-df-skein-relation","Skein Relation"],"display":"df-skein-relation — Skein Relation","depends_on":["[[../batch19/58-df-laurent-polynomial.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-skein-relation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-skein-relation</span><span>Skein Relation</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-skein-relation — Skein Relation"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"646322422ec21b3d\" href=\"?note=646322422ec21b3d\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-laurent-polynomial.md\">../batch19/58-df-laurent-polynomial.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L,L_+,L_-,L_0,\\Phi,P,+_P,\\cdot_P,0_P,1_P,a_+,a_-,z\\in V\">\\(\\mathcal L,L_+,L_-,L_0,\\Phi,P,+_P,\\cdot_P,0_P,1_P,a_+,a_-,z\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\langle1,0\\rangle,\\langle-1,0\\rangle,\\langle0,1\\rangle\\in\\mathbb Z^2\">\\(\\langle1,0\\rangle,\\langle-1,0\\rangle,\\langle0,1\\rangle\\in\\mathbb Z^2\\)</span> are the exponent vectors for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a,a^{-1},z\">\\(a,a^{-1},z\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LaurentPolynomialRingStructure}_S\\subseteq V^{11}\">\\(\\mathrm{LaurentPolynomialRingStructure}_S\\subseteq V^{11}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\\subseteq V^9\">\\(\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\\subseteq V^9\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"646322422ec21b3d\" href=\"?note=646322422ec21b3d\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-laurent-polynomial.md\">../batch19/58-df-laurent-polynomial.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HOMFLYPTSkein}_S\\subseteq V^{13}\">\\(\\mathrm{HOMFLYPTSkein}_S\\subseteq V^{13}\\)</span> (ring-explicit skein predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}skein\\text{-}relation}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{HOMFLYPTSkein}_S\n(\\Phi,\\mathcal L,L_+,L_-,L_0;P,+_P,\\cdot_P,0_P,1_P,a_+,a_-,z)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{LaurentPolynomialRingStructure}_S\n(P,+_P,\\cdot_P,0_P,1_P,\\mathbb Z,+_{\\mathbb Z},\\cdot_{\\mathbb Z},0_{\\mathbb Z},1_{\\mathbb Z},2)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\n(a_+,1_{\\mathbb Z},\\langle1,0\\rangle,\\mathbb Z,+_{\\mathbb Z},\\cdot_{\\mathbb Z},0_{\\mathbb Z},1_{\\mathbb Z},2)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\n(a_-,1_{\\mathbb Z},\\langle-1,0\\rangle,\\mathbb Z,+_{\\mathbb Z},\\cdot_{\\mathbb Z},0_{\\mathbb Z},1_{\\mathbb Z},2)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\n(z,1_{\\mathbb Z},\\langle0,1\\rangle,\\mathbb Z,+_{\\mathbb Z},\\cdot_{\\mathbb Z},0_{\\mathbb Z},1_{\\mathbb Z},2)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\Phi,\\mathcal L,P)\n\\land L_+,L_-,L_0\\in\\mathcal L\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\cdot_P(a_+,\\Phi(L_+))\n=+_P\\bigl(\\cdot_P(a_-,\\Phi(L_-)),\\cdot_P(z,\\Phi(L_0))\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}skein\\text{-}relation}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{HOMFLYPTSkein}_S\n(\\Phi,\\mathcal L,L_+,L_-,L_0;P,+_P,\\cdot_P,0_P,1_P,a_+,a_-,z)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{LaurentPolynomialRingStructure}_S\n(P,+_P,\\cdot_P,0_P,1_P,\\mathbb Z,+_{\\mathbb Z},\\cdot_{\\mathbb Z},0_{\\mathbb Z},1_{\\mathbb Z},2)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\n(a_+,1_{\\mathbb Z},\\langle1,0\\rangle,\\mathbb Z,+_{\\mathbb Z},\\cdot_{\\mathbb Z},0_{\\mathbb Z},1_{\\mathbb Z},2)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\n(a_-,1_{\\mathbb Z},\\langle-1,0\\rangle,\\mathbb Z,+_{\\mathbb Z},\\cdot_{\\mathbb Z},0_{\\mathbb Z},1_{\\mathbb Z},2)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\n(z,1_{\\mathbb Z},\\langle0,1\\rangle,\\mathbb Z,+_{\\mathbb Z},\\cdot_{\\mathbb Z},0_{\\mathbb Z},1_{\\mathbb Z},2)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\Phi,\\mathcal L,P)\n\\land L_+,L_-,L_0\\in\\mathcal L\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\cdot_P(a_+,\\Phi(L_+))\n=+_P\\bigl(\\cdot_P(a_-,\\Phi(L_-)),\\cdot_P(z,\\Phi(L_0))\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Skein: relation between link diagrams differing at one crossing</li>\n<li>The subtraction form <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"aP(L_+)-a^{-1}P(L_-)=zP(L_0)\">\\(aP(L_+)-a^{-1}P(L_-)=zP(L_0)\\)</span> is written equivalently as <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"aP(L_+)=a^{-1}P(L_-)+zP(L_0)\">\\(aP(L_+)=a^{-1}P(L_-)+zP(L_0)\\)</span>, avoiding an unsourced subtraction operator.</li>\n<li>The coefficient object is the two-variable Laurent-polynomial ring, not the ordinary polynomial carrier with exponent set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb N^2\">\\(\\mathbb N^2\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>HOMFLY and Kauffman bracket skein relations are parallel specializations of this pattern.</li>\n<li>Jones: from Kauffman bracket with specific substitution</li>\n<li>Skein algebra: span of diagrams modulo skein relation</li>\n<li>TQFT: skein relations arise from flat connections</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Jones, Hecke algebras and representation of braid groups</li>\n<li>Kauffman, State models and the Jones polynomial</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch19/58-df-laurent-polynomial.md","status":"resolved","id":"646322422ec21b3d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-laurent-polynomial.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch19/58-df-laurent-polynomial.md","status":"resolved","id":"646322422ec21b3d","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{LaurentPolynomialRingStructure}_S\\subseteq V^{11}$ and $\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\\subseteq V^9$ (see [[../batch19/58-df-laurent-polynomial.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3$ (see [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathcal L,L_+,L_-,L_0,\\Phi,P,+_P,\\cdot_P,0_P,1_P,a_+,a_-,z\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\langle1,0\\rangle,\\langle-1,0\\rangle,\\langle0,1\\rangle\\in\\mathbb Z^2","display":false},{"tex":"a,a^{-1},z","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LaurentPolynomialRingStructure}_S\\subseteq V^{11}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\\subseteq V^9","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HOMFLYPTSkein}_S\\subseteq V^{13}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}skein\\text{-}relation}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{HOMFLYPTSkein}_S\n(\\Phi,\\mathcal L,L_+,L_-,L_0;P,+_P,\\cdot_P,0_P,1_P,a_+,a_-,z)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&\n\\mathrm{LaurentPolynomialRingStructure}_S\n(P,+_P,\\cdot_P,0_P,1_P,\\mathbb Z,+_{\\mathbb Z},\\cdot_{\\mathbb Z},0_{\\mathbb Z},1_{\\mathbb Z},2)\\\\\n&\\land\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\n(a_+,1_{\\mathbb Z},\\langle1,0\\rangle,\\mathbb Z,+_{\\mathbb Z},\\cdot_{\\mathbb Z},0_{\\mathbb Z},1_{\\mathbb Z},2)\\\\\n&\\land\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\n(a_-,1_{\\mathbb Z},\\langle-1,0\\rangle,\\mathbb Z,+_{\\mathbb Z},\\cdot_{\\mathbb Z},0_{\\mathbb Z},1_{\\mathbb Z},2)\\\\\n&\\land\\mathrm{LaurentMonomial}_S\n(z,1_{\\mathbb Z},\\langle0,1\\rangle,\\mathbb Z,+_{\\mathbb Z},\\cdot_{\\mathbb Z},0_{\\mathbb Z},1_{\\mathbb Z},2)\\\\\n&\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\Phi,\\mathcal L,P)\n\\land L_+,L_-,L_0\\in\\mathcal L\\\\\n&\\land\\cdot_P(a_+,\\Phi(L_+))\n=+_P\\bigl(\\cdot_P(a_-,\\Phi(L_-)),\\cdot_P(z,\\Phi(L_0))\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"aP(L_+)-a^{-1}P(L_-)=zP(L_0)","display":false},{"tex":"aP(L_+)=a^{-1}P(L_-)+zP(L_0)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb N^2","display":false}],"bytes":2588,"backlinks":[{"id":"dcafe9320aa6f056","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{HOMFLYPTSkein}_S\\subseteq V^{13}$ (see [[58-df-skein-relation]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1183","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-skein-relation.md|58-df-skein-relation]]（batch05）"}],"outgoing":["646322422ec21b3d","36d7463d215be751"]}